    "question": "A plumber bought 10 meters of copper and 5 more meters of plastic pipe. If each meter cost $4, how much did the plumber spent on the copper and plastic pipe?",
    "gold": "100",
    "answer": "He bought 10 + 5 = <<10+5=15>>15 meters of plastic pipe.\nThe total meters of the copper and plastic pipe is 10 + 15 = <<10+15=25>>25.\nThe plumber spent $4 x 25 = $<<4*25=100>>100 on copper and plastic pipe.\n#### 100"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much the plumber spent on the copper and plastic pipe, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total length of the plastic pipe.\n2. Calculate the total cost of the copper pipe.\n3. Calculate the total cost of the plastic pipe.\n4. Add the total cost of the copper pipe and the total cost of the plastic pipe to get the final amount spent.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. The plumber bought 10 meters of copper pipe.\n2. The plumber also bought 5 more meters of plastic pipe than copper pipe. Therefore, the length of the plastic pipe is:\n   \\[\n   10 + 5 = 15 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total cost of the copper pipe:\n3. The cost of each meter of copper pipe is $4. Therefore, the total cost of the copper pipe is:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ meters} \\times 4 \\text{ dollars/meter} = 40 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nThen, we calculate the total cost of the plastic pipe:\n4. The cost of each meter of plastic pipe is $4. Therefore, the total cost of the plastic pipe is:\n   \\[\n   15 \\text{ meters} \\times 4 \\text{ dollars/meter} = 60 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nFinally, we add the total cost of the copper pipe and the total cost of the plastic pipe to get the final amount spent:\n5. The total amount spent is:\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ dollars} + 60 \\text{ dollars} = 100 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the plumber spent \\(\\boxed{100}\\) dollars on the copper and plastic pipe.",
